---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How to Measure Grip Size — Pickleball Paddle Guide | PaddleFitHub"
  description="Learn the Vernier method to measure your hand for the perfect pickleball paddle grip size. Step-by-step instructions with diagrams."
  canonicalPath="/blog/how-to-measure-grip-size/"
>
  <div class="container-narrow py-16">
    <p class="text-caption-mono text-mute uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Resource</p>
    <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink mb-4">How to Measure Grip Size</h1>
    <p class="text-body-lg text-body mb-8">The Vernier method is the standard way pickleball and tennis pros measure for grip size. Here is how to do it.</p>

    <div class="prose text-body-md text-body space-y-6 max-w-none">
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Step 1: Find the crease</h2>
      <p>Hold your paddle hand open, palm facing up. Look for the middle crease that runs across your palm (the proximal palmar crease). This is the crease closest to your fingers, not the one near your wrist.</p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Step 2: Measure from crease to fingertip</h2>
      <p>Using a ruler or measuring tape, measure from the middle crease to the tip of your ring finger. This is your hand measurement.</p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Step 3: Match to grip size</h2>
      <p>Your measurement directly corresponds to a standard grip size:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>4" or less → 4" grip</li>
        <li>4" – 4⅛" → 4⅛" grip</li>
        <li>4⅛" – 4¼" → 4¼" grip</li>
        <li>4¼" – 4⅜" → 4⅜" grip</li>
        <li>4⅜" – 4½" → 4½" grip</li>
        <li>4½" – 4⅝" → 4⅝" grip</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Tips for accuracy</h2>
      <p>Measure twice. If you fall between sizes, size down and add an overgrip (each overgrip adds roughly ⅛"). Use the <a href="/tools/grip-size-calculator/">Grip Size Calculator</a> for a precise recommendation with comfort adjustments.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
      <a href="/tools/grip-size-calculator/" class="btn-primary">Try the Grip Size Calculator</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>